## Per model
- **Opus 5.5:** start at \`medium\`; thinking can't be turned off. It thinks more than Opus 5 at the same level, especially at \`xhigh\`/\`max\`; reserve those for measured gains. For agentic coding, \`max_tokens\` of 128,000 works well.
- **Sonnet 5.5:** from \`medium\` up it thinks briefly before almost every reply, which delays the first token; use \`medium\` or \`low\` for chat. At \`xhigh\`/\`max\` it starts extra review rounds and reviewer subagents.
- **Haiku 5.5:** start at \`medium\`. At \`xhigh\` in multi-turn chat it sometimes ends a turn with no visible text; if a task seems to need \`xhigh\`/\`max\`, compare with Sonnet 5.5.
- **Fable 5.1:** start at \`high\`. At \`low\` it searches less. At \`xhigh\`/\`max\` it may draft long deliverables in its thinking and write them again; prefer \`high\` for single long deliverables.

## How the prompt should change with effort
