<models>
# Target models (Gemini, lineup checked 2026-11-08)

Thinking is always on and is set with \`thinking_level\`; supported levels differ per model.

| Model | ID | Positioning | Price (input / output per MTok) | Thinking levels | Default |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Gemini 4 Argon | \`gemini-4-argon\` | Flagship reasoning model for deep work: coding, finance, legal, security, science. Unified 1,048,576-token limit for input plus output. | $2 / $10 until 2026-11-30, then $4 / $20 | \`low\` \`medium\` \`high\` | \`medium\` |
| Gemini 3.8 Flash | \`gemini-3.8-flash\` | Newest and most intelligent Flash model. | $0.75 / $3.75 until 2026-12-31, then $1.50 / $7.50 | \`low\` \`medium\` \`high\` | \`medium\` |
| Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite | \`gemini-3.5-flash-lite\` | Fastest and most cost-effective 3.5 model, for high-throughput work. | $0.30 / $2.50 | \`minimal\` \`low\` \`medium\` \`high\` | \`minimal\` |

Thinking tokens are billed as output.
Deprecated \`gemini-2.5-pro\` and \`gemini-2.5-flash\` route to 3.8 Flash and 3.5 Flash-Lite on 2026-12-01.

## Choosing a model
- **Gemini 4 Argon** for genuinely hard reasoning, very large inputs read at once, and very long single outputs. Thinking can't be turned off.
- **Gemini 3.8 Flash** for long-running software engineering, autonomous agents and complex enterprise workflows.
- **Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite** for simple, mechanical or high-volume work: classification, extraction, routing, short answers, quick transformations.
- For a short factual question or a one-line transformation, Flash-Lite at \`minimal\` is enough; a stronger model adds cost, not quality.
</models>

