<surface name="API">
# Surface: Gemini API / system instruction

The output is the **system instruction** for an application calling the Gemini API (Google AI Studio or Vertex AI). It applies to the entire request and across user and model turns, so it must hold up across many inputs.

How to write it:
- Start with role and product context, then behavioral constraints and the output format; Google advises putting these first.
- Define the inputs the application will send, how they are delimited and how to handle missing data. Mark runtime values with placeholders; Vertex AI prompt templates use single braces, e.g. \`{current_date}\`.
- State the rules and the fixed response for off-topic requests and missing information. System instructions don't fully prevent jailbreaks or leaks: keep secrets out and add safeguards for untrusted input.
- For grounded apps, restrict answers to the provided context and say what to do when the information is missing.
- Include a few consistently formatted examples when format or tone is subtle.
- Keep the static part first and unchanged so requests share a cached prefix.
- If the application parses JSON, structured output (\`response_schema\`) enforces the schema.

API settings:
- \`generateContent\`: \`system_instruction\`, and \`thinking_level\` in the generation config. \`thinking_budget\` and \`MINIMAL\` are rejected on Argon.
- Remove \`temperature\`, \`top_p\`, \`top_k\` for Gemini 4 and 3.6+; \`frequency_penalty\`, \`presence_penalty\` and \`candidate_count\` are rejected on Argon.
- Argon's default single-request output is 65,536 tokens when streaming and 32,768 otherwise; longer outputs use long decodes on \`v1beta1\`.
- Prefilled model turns are not supported on Argon; history can't end with a model turn.
</surface>

<candidates>
Recommend only from these models. The effort must be one the chosen model supports, in that model's own scale.
- \`gemini-4-argon\` — Gemini 4 Argon (Google) · levels: low | medium | high, default \`medium\` · $4 / $20 per MTok
- \`gemini-3.8-flash\` — Gemini 3.8 Flash (Google) · levels: low | medium | high, default \`medium\` · $1.5 / $7.5 per MTok
- \`gemini-3.5-flash-lite\` — Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite (Google) · levels: minimal | low | medium | high, default \`minimal\` · $0.3 / $2.5 per MTok
</candidates>

